      "year_built_as_surveyed": "1971",
      "architect_as_surveyed": "Bulkley & Sazevich",
      "note": "Friendship Village by Bulkley & Sazevich, in the Western Addition A-2 redevelopment area, which kept a Victorian-era facade as a gateway into its central courtyard. The complex has the massing, flat roof and regular fenestration of a Late Modernist building, with shingle siding nodding to the Third Bay Tradition. The old facade survives, now closed off by a security gate."
